Package: mediamix
Title: Media Transforms and Attribution Path Construction
Version: 0.4.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Justin", "Chase", , "jchase.msu@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Feature engineering for marketing mix modelling and multi-touch
    attribution. Converts raw media spend into carryover- and
    saturation-adjusted regressors using geometric, delayed and Weibull
    adstock kernels and four saturation curves, and converts raw event logs
    into model-ready customer journeys with rule-based and Markov
    removal-effect attribution. Marginal return on investment is computed by
    counterfactual simulation through the full transform.
    Carryover parameters are selected by cross-validation against an actual
    key performance indicator using a user-supplied model, rather than by a
    heuristic. The core transforms are plain R functions on numeric vectors,
    and the only non-base dependencies are 'cli', 'rlang' and 'data.table';
    optional 'recipes' steps and 'dials' parameter objects support joint
    tuning of carryover, saturation and model hyperparameters. Adstock
    methods follow Broadbent (1979, Journal of the Market Research Society,
    21(3), 139-166) and Jin et al. (2017, Google Inc.,
    <https://research.google/pubs/pub46001/>); saturation curves
    follow Hill (1910, The Journal of Physiology, 40, iv-vii); Markov
    attribution follows Anderl et al. (2016) <doi:10.1016/j.ijresmar.2016.03.001>.
